**Why this improves the score:**
- If the longest-path model matches the simulator exactly, each neighborhood evaluation drops from an expensive oracle call to an O(n + conflicts) computation, enabling ~100x more 2-opt/or-opt/reversal/ILS iterations → deeper local optima → lower makespan.
- The calibration step guarantees we never trust a wrong model: final cost is always computed with the real oracle, and a mismatch triggers an oracle-based re-polish.
- Even in fallback mode, the tuple-keyed oracle cache eliminates redundant evaluations, and the added ruin-and-recreate neighborhood plus adaptive perturbation strength diversify the search.
